# CodeMind Academy — Environment Variables
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values.
# NEVER commit .env to Git.

# ── Database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SQLite connection string (used by Prisma)
# For production, switch to PostgreSQL:
#   DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/codemind
DATABASE_URL="file:./db/custom.db"

# ── Application ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Public URL of the deployed application (used for referral links, etc.)
NEXT_PUBLIC_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# ── Authentication ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The auth system uses cookie-based sessions stored in the database.
# No JWT_SECRET is required for the current implementation.
# If you switch to JWT, add: JWT_SECRET="your-super-secret-key-change-this"

# ── AI / LLM (z-ai-web-dev-sdk) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# The z-ai-web-dev-sdk is configured automatically in the sandbox environment.
# For production deployment, ensure the SDK credentials are available.
# No additional env vars are needed — the SDK handles auth internally.

# ── Payment Methods (Informational only — manual verification) ──────────────
# These are displayed in the UI. No payment gateway integration exists.
# INSTAPAY, VODAFONE_CASH, ETISALAT_CASH are the supported manual methods.

# ── Branding (Optional overrides — defaults in src/lib/brand.ts) ─────────────
# The following can be overridden in the database Settings table via Admin UI:
# - brand_name
# - brand_tagline
# - whatsapp_teacher
# - whatsapp_technical
# - whatsapp_subscription
# - academic_year
# - price_monthly, price_3months, price_6months, price_early_bird
